&lt;/ul&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[Spring Framework 6.2.18 and 7.0.7 Available Now]]></title><link>https://spring.io/blog/2026/04/17/spring-framework-6-2-18-and-7-0-7-available-now</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://spring.io/blog/2026/04/17/spring-framework-6-2-18-and-7-0-7-available-now</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[snicoll]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Apr 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;On behalf of the team and everyone who has contributed, I am pleased to announce that Spring Framework &lt;code&gt;6.2.18&lt;/code&gt; and  &lt;code&gt;7.0.7&lt;/code&gt; are available now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Spring Framework &lt;code&gt;6.2.18&lt;/code&gt; ships with &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v6.2.18&quot;&gt;27 fixes and documentation improvements&lt;/a&gt;. This version will be shipped next week with Spring Boot &lt;code&gt;3.5.14&lt;/code&gt;.
Spring Framework &lt;code&gt;7.0.7&lt;/code&gt; ships with &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/releases/tag/v7.0.7&quot;&gt;52 fixes and documentation improvements&lt;/a&gt;. This version will be shipped next week with Spring Boot &lt;code&gt;4.0.6&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;cve-reports&quot; style=&quot;position:relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#cve-reports&quot; aria-label=&quot;cve reports permalink&quot; class=&quot;anchor before&quot;&gt;&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; focusable=&quot;false&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; version=&quot;1.1&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 16 16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&quot;evenodd&quot; d=&quot;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;CVE Reports:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This release addresses:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-22740&quot;&gt;CVE-2026-22740&lt;/a&gt; &quot;Spring Framework DoS with Multipart Temp Files in WebFlux&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-22741&quot;&gt;CVE-2026-22741&lt;/a&gt; &quot;Static resource cache poisoning in Spring MVC and WebFlux&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-22745&quot;&gt;CVE-2026-22745&lt;/a&gt; &quot;Denial of service in static resource handling on Windows platforms&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open source support for Spring Framework 5.3.x and 6.1.x generations has ended, see &lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/projects/spring-framework#support&quot;&gt;our support page for more information&lt;/a&gt;.
This fix has been applied to the 5.3.46 and 6.1.24 commercial releases, available now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are not a commercial customer, &lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/projects/spring-framework/#support&quot;&gt;please consider upgrading to an open source supported version&lt;/a&gt; at your earliest convenience.
Commercial customers using Spring Boot 2.7, 3.1, or 3.2 can make use of Spring Boot Hotfix releases 2.7.32.1, 3.3.18.1 and 3.4.15.1. Releases are available now on the Spring commercial artifact repository and can be accessed with a &lt;a href=&quot;https://enterprise.spring.io&quot;&gt;Spring Enterprise Subscription&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/projects/spring-framework/&quot;&gt;Project Page&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework&quot;&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-framework/issues&quot;&gt;Issues&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/reference/&quot;&gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Bootiful Podcast: the legendary Craig Walls]]></title><link>https://spring.io/blog/2026/04/16/a-bootiful-podcast-craig-walls</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://spring.io/blog/2026/04/16/a-bootiful-podcast-craig-walls</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[joshlong]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 16 Apr 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;Hi Spring fans! In this installment we talk to the legendary Craig Walls, author of &lt;em&gt;Spring In Action&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;Spring AI in Action&lt;/em&gt;, and more!&lt;/p&gt;
